    "created_at": "2023-04-16T12:02:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-04-16T13:27:43Z",
    "body": "> There was some discussion around deprecating dialog.show() in favor of <dialog popover> which would address this issue.\r\n\r\nI would think it makes things easier for developers to distinguish between (and correctly use) dialogs and popovers if `<dialog>` would always be modal and `popover` always be non-modal. \r\n\r\n> Should we rename popovertarget to openabletarget (or whatever), and allow it to work with other things that can be open/closed, such as `<dialog>` and `<details>`?\r\n\r\nI think this makes sense (including `popovertargetaction` ➡️ `openabletargetaction`, or something more bikeshedded). ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1510352910/reactions",
