    "created_at": "2023-04-17T13:19:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-04-17T13:19:59Z",
    "body": "At the risk of sparking debate on the particulars, a modal dialog is effectively a navigation to a smaller page. I don’t think it is any more drastic of a shift than a page navigation. Conversely expecting people to write JavaScript to wire up a button can create inconsistencies with interactions which results in arguably more frustrating consequences, for example missing out on one of the Enter/Space/Click/Touch actions (I literally had a bug report today regarding exactly this issue).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1511334873/reactions",
